 "applies_to": "Carrier 50 Series water source heat pumps (50WC, 50WD, 50WT, 50HQP, 50VQP) with the factory TruVu TV-WSHP controller.",
 "summary": "The TV-WSHP is a TruVu controller for Carrier 50 Series water source heat pumps. It speaks BACnet IP only on dual Ethernet ports; an MS/TP network needs a TruVu Compact Router (TV-CRB-E2). The table has 184 objects, including two sets of Unit Protection Module (UPM) data for stage 1 and stage 2 compressors, network inputs for space temperature, RH and CO2, and a BV per alarm.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "This is the TruVu generation; the older WSHP Open v3 controller has its own list.",
  "State texts are re-keyed from the Units column of the table (e.g. 0=Off, 1=On). MV 6100 lists states 1-16; MV 6200, 6101 and 6201 are printed as the same states as MV 6100.",
  "Stage 2 UPM points only apply to two-stage or two-compressor units.",
  "Space Temp Source (MV 2003) is printed with states 1, 3, 4, 6 and 7 only."
 ],
